From: Local MSM8916 Buildroot integration
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve UTF-8 byte sequences when quoting shell fragments

Escaping non-ASCII bytes in UTF-8 paths inserts backslashes inside code
points, making pkg-config output undecodable by Meson. Shell metacharacters
are ASCII; apply the existing escaping policy only to ASCII bytes. This also
avoids signed-char values being classified as control characters.

Upstream: Not submitted (local host compatibility fix for pkgconf 2.3.0)
--- a/libpkgconf/fragment.c
+++ b/libpkgconf/fragment.c
@@ -463,7 +463,8 @@ fragment_quote(const pkgconf_fragment_t *frag)
 
 	for (; *src; src++)
 	{
-		if (((*src < ' ') ||
+		/* Shell metacharacters are ASCII; keep UTF-8 byte sequences intact. */
+		if ((unsigned char)*src < 0x80 && ((*src < ' ') ||
 		    (*src >= (' ' + (frag->merged ? 1 : 0)) && *src < '$') ||
 		    (*src > '$' && *src < '(') ||
 		    (*src > ')' && *src < '+') ||
